       }
      ],
      "text": "Tamsulosin CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " hypersensitivity (rxns have included rash, urticaria, pruritus, angioedema and resp Sx). Caution w a serious or life-threatening sulfa allergy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tamsulosin:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉w strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (eg, ketoconazole); caution w mod CYP3A4 inhibitors (eg, erythromycin), CYP2D6 inhibitors (eg, paroxetine, terbinafine) or in CYP2D6 poor metabolizers, esp above 0.4 mg. ⍉w other α blockers. Caution w PDE5 inhibitors (both are vasodilators; together they can cause Sxtomatic hypotension) and w warfarin."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "B4 cataract or glaucoma surg, tell the ophthalmologist about tamsulosin: intraoperative floppy iris syndrome has been seen in some pts on or previously treated w alpha-1 blockers. Starting it when that surg = scheduled = ⍉recommended."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Postural hypotension Sx such as dizziness: caution w driving, operating machinery or hazardous tasks."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tamsulosin OD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " support the cardiovasc system first (supine position; if that isn't enough, consider IVF; then vasopressors if needed), and monitor and support renal funct. Dialysis = unlikely to help (94% to 99% protein bound)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
